The "connection collision" last-reset on router1 and "no path" on router2 are both one-time startup artifacts: when both BGP daemons start simultaneously, two competing TCP connections race; BGP collision detection (RFC 4271 §6.8) drops one, the surviving connection establishes normally. The FRR log confirms exactly that — no subsequent resets in 3+ minutes.

No mechanism exists for periodic drops: no flap script, no carrier changes, no hold-timer expiry, no tc rules dropping keepalives, no resource pressure.

